sequenceDiagram
    participant User as User / kubectl
    participant KubeAPI as kube-apiserver<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Webhook as training-operator Webhook<br/>9443/TCP HTTPS TLS (self-signed CA)
    participant Operator as training-operator Controller<br/>controller-runtime
    participant Pods as Worker/Master Pods<br/>User Namespace
    participant Svc as Headless Services<br/>User Namespace
    participant NetPol as NetworkPolicies<br/>User Namespace
    participant Prometheus as Prometheus<br/>openshift-monitoring

    Note over User,KubeAPI: Flow 1: Training Job Lifecycle

    User->>KubeAPI: POST PyTorchJob/TFJob/MPIJob/...<br/>Auth: User token/kubeconfig
    KubeAPI->>Webhook: POST /validate-kubeflow-org-v1-*<br/>HTTPS 9443/TCP TLS (self-signed CA)<br/>Auth: Kubernetes admission
    Webhook-->>KubeAPI: Admission Response (allow/deny)
    KubeAPI-->>User: Job created / rejected

    Note over Operator,KubeAPI: Controller reconciliation loop

    KubeAPI->>Operator: Watch event (CRD change)<br/>HTTPS 6443/TCP TLS 1.2+<br/>Auth: ServiceAccount token
    Operator->>KubeAPI: Create worker/master Pods<br/>HTTPS 6443/TCP TLS 1.2+
    KubeAPI-->>Pods: Pods scheduled and started
    Operator->>KubeAPI: Create Headless Services<br/>HTTPS 6443/TCP TLS 1.2+
    KubeAPI-->>Svc: Services created

    alt PyTorchJob only
        Operator->>KubeAPI: Create NetworkPolicy<br/>HTTPS 6443/TCP TLS 1.2+
        KubeAPI-->>NetPol: NetworkPolicy applied<br/>Allow intra-job + monitoring
    end

    Note over Operator,Pods: Lifecycle management

    Operator->>KubeAPI: Track replica status<br/>HTTPS 6443/TCP
    Operator->>KubeAPI: Handle restarts/failures<br/>HTTPS 6443/TCP
    Operator->>KubeAPI: Cleanup completed jobs<br/>DELETE pods/services/netpols

    Note over Prometheus,Operator: Flow 2: Metrics Collection

    Prometheus->>Operator: GET /metrics<br/>HTTP 8080/TCP TLS (cluster profile)<br/>Auth: None (PodMonitor)
    Operator-->>Prometheus: Prometheus metrics response
